    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lean heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** and **Drake Baldwin** to anchor the lineup today. **Gunnar Henderson** holds the highest efficiency score at 72.53, despite a challenging matchup against the left-handed Lopez; his elite base projection and favorable park factors outweigh the platoon drag. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** is a top-tier play at 71.33. Leading off against Sugano, he benefits from a weak 4.91 xERA opponent and a significant +19% boost due to the pitcher\u2019s lack of skill, making him an ideal source of production today. Note, however, that **Drake Baldwin** carries a 33% rain risk, so monitor the stadium forecast closely leading up to first pitch. **Coby Mayo** also emerges as a high-upside play at 66.72, as his ability to handle left-handed pitching allows him to capitalize on the weak matchup against Lopez despite his lower spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Miguel Vargas**, who posted a competitive 49.24 score. While his xwOBA of .389 is impressive and he provides value in our critical pursuit of stolen bases, his raw efficiency fell just short of the starters, particularly against the respectable 3.89 xERA of Kremer. Consequently, **Miguel Vargas** remains on the pine to preserve game caps in favor of higher-floor plays like **Heliot Ramos**, whose 62.17 score is bolstered by a favorable platoon advantage against Sandoval. Elsewhere, we continue to manage the health of our depth, as **Jordan Westburg** and **Andy Pages** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** as the odd man out of the active rotation today. Keep a close eye on the confirmed lineups for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**, as their projected efficiency is predicated on the assumed order against Lopez; any drop in their lineup placement will trigger a re-evaluation of their utility.",
